<title>UK: MSAS lifts stake in Hugarian unit to 100pct.</title>
<headline>MSAS lifts stake in Hugarian unit to 100pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK-based global freight forwarder, MSAS Cargo International Ltd said it has acquired the outstanding 42.3 percent of MSAS Cargo Budapest Ltd.</p>
<p>The now wholly-owned Hungarian subsidiary, managed by Lajos Toth, will report to and have full support for systems, staff training and dvelopment, operational procedures and finance from MSAS Germany, it added in a statement.</p>
<p>MSAS has been able to acquire its stake following the recent change in Hungarian laws allowing 100 percent ownership by a foreign entity, the statement said.</p>
</text>
